      "text": "To find the area of a square, we first need to understand the relationship between its side length and the perimeter. The perimeter is the total length of all sides combined. In a square, this is simply four times one side’s length because a square has four equal sides.\n\nGiven the perimeter is 32 feet, we can set up the equation based on this information:\n\nPerimeter = 4 * Side*\n32 ft = 4 * [Side*]\n\nNow, solve for [Side*] by dividing both sides of the equation by 4:\n\nSide*\n= 32 ft / 4\n= 8 ft\n\nNow that we have the side length, we can calculate the square area using the formula for area of a square, which is Side* squared:\n\nArea = [Side*]^2\n= (8 ft)^2\n= 64 square feet\n\nThus, the area of the square with a perimeter of 32 feet is boxed as 64 square feet.",
